# Testing

- User-visible happy paths are English Gherkin in `features/*.feature`, bound by
  `backend/tests/bdd/` through the HTTP API and shared steps. Follow
  `features/README.md`; keep scenarios deterministic, without network or LLM calls.
- Validation, boundaries and error cases belong in the area's existing unit test
  file using its helpers. Test names are sentences. Agent-hook contracts live in
  `scripts/test_agent_rules.py` and run without the backend or database.
- Red first: run new scenarios and tests without the change, see the intended
  failure, then implement it. Report that evidence in the PR.
- A new route needs a probe in `backend/tests/route_isolation/` or an entry with a reason in
  `EXEMPT` of `backend/tests/test_route_isolation_sweep.py`, which fails for every unclassified
  `METHOD /path`; a changed route keeps its probe truthful.
- Treat the shared test DB as single-writer: never run two backend test processes
  at once, and not while `scripts/dev-local.sh` uses the same database. Use only the test
  database and compose commands in AGENTS.md. The database keeps the Alembic head of the last
  run; when setup fails with `No such revision`, another branch's migrations are applied, and
  `docker compose -f infra/docker-compose.declaration-test.yml restart postgres` recreates the
  in-memory database (only while no other run is active; interim until #75).
- Iterate selectively (`cd backend && uv run pytest tests/test_x.py -k name`
  or `cd frontend && npm test -- <file>`); the whole backend suite takes about 30 minutes.
  Run `make lint` before a push and `make test` before a merge; `make test-agent-rules` needs no DB.
